From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: acqxi <kacqxi@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 08:02:41 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 09/12] Performance metrics in the usage dashboard
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Server: server.getUsagePerformance reads finished provider turns with
  turn performance from the projection store (provider thread for the
  driver, run for the requested model when the provider reported none),
  keeps those that started in the dashboard's window (the same day and
  time-zone rules as the usage summary, instants when hourly), applies the
  usage model aliases, and groups them by usage provider and model: turn
  count, generation tokens and time of turns with at least 1 s of
  generation, whether any count was estimated, and the TTFT and TTFA
  samples. Diagnostics read scope, like the usage summary.
- Web: the Model breakdown gains tok/s (token-weighted, ≈ when
  estimated), median TTFT and TTFA (p90 in the tooltip) and measured
  turns, merged across the selected environments before the medians.
  Models T3 never timed, such as those only found by the usage scan, show
  a dash. The columns show from the lg breakpoint.
